1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
(a + b)² = a² + 2ab + b². But where does the 2ab come from?

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:03,200
Start with one square. Its side is a plus b.

3
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:05,600
So the whole area is (a + b) squared.

4
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:07,200
Now cut it once across and once down.

5
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:10,400
Four pieces: a², a times b, a times b, and b². That is the entire formula.

6
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:12,000
(a + b)² = a² + 2ab + b². And those two rectangles are identical.

7
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,400
Rotate one onto the other and it fits exactly. Same rectangle, twice — there is your 2ab.

8
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:16,000
(a + b)² is NOT a² + b². This is the mistake everyone makes.

9
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:18,400
Leave out the 2ab and the square has a hole in it.

10
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,000
Same square. Just call the sides x and h instead.

11
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,400
(x + h)² = x² + 2xh + h². Now let h get small.

12
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:24,000
The corner h² is a speck. The growth is the two strips: 2xh.

13
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,000
So x² grows at 2x. That is the derivative of x squared — and it is the same square.

14
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,800
You memorised this in school. Nobody showed you it was a square. Follow for the math behind AI — @observer.collapse
